## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

### Summary

**10 tests — 9 Critical findings, 1 Medium**

This suite is the textbook example of **coverage-touching**: every public method on `ProductCatalog` is called (yielding ~95% line coverage), but almost nothing is actually verified. 6 of 10 tests have **zero assertions**, and the 4 that do assert only check `IsNotNull` — a trivially-passing bar that verifies no business logic.

---

### 🔴 CRITICAL

#### 1. Systematic Coverage-Touching (entire file)

Every public method is called in declaration order with no meaningful verification. This is the #1 reason you're finding production bugs despite high coverage numbers.

#### 2. No Assertions — 6 tests (lines 17–21, 32–36, 39–43, 63–66, 68–74, 85–88)

| Test | What it calls | What it verifies |
|------|--------------|-------------------|
| `AddProduct_Works` | `AddProduct()` | ❌ Nothing |
| `UpdatePrice_Works` | `UpdatePrice()` | ❌ Nothing |
| `RemoveProduct_Works` | `RemoveProduct()` | ❌ Nothing |
| `GetProductCount_Works` | `GetProductCount()` | ❌ Nothing |
| `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` | `ApplyBulkDiscount()` | ❌ Nothing |
| `ImportFromCsv_Works` | `ImportFromCsv()` | ❌ Nothing |

These tests pass even if the methods silently do nothing.

**Fix** (example for `AddProduct_Works`):
```csharp
// BEFORE
[TestMethod]
public void AddProduct_Works()
{
    var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
    _catalog.AddProduct(product);
}

// AFTER
[TestMethod]
public void AddProduct_ThenProductIsRetrievable()
{
    var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
    _catalog.AddProduct(product);

    var retrieved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual("Widget", retrieved?.Name);
    Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, retrieved?.Price);
}
```

**Fix** (example for `UpdatePrice_Works`):
```csharp
// AFTER
[TestMethod]
public void UpdatePrice_ChangesTheStoredPrice()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    _catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);

    var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated?.Price);
}
```

**Fix** (example for `RemoveProduct_Works`):
```csharp
// AFTER
[TestMethod]
public void RemoveProduct_MakesProductUnretrievable()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    _catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");

    Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
